Subject: [PATCH] ggml-rpc: correct stale GGML_OP_COUNT static assert

The pinned ggml (135ce1e) defines 101 ops in the ggml_op enum, but
ggml-rpc.h still asserts GGML_OP_COUNT == 105, a stale value left over
from an earlier sync. Correct the guard so the RPC backend compiles.

--- a/ggml/include/ggml-rpc.h
+++ b/ggml/include/ggml-rpc.h
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 #define RPC_PROTO_PATCH_VERSION 3
 
 #ifdef  __cplusplus
-static_assert(GGML_OP_COUNT == 105, "GGML_OP_COUNT has changed - update RPC_PROTO_PATCH_VERSION");
+static_assert(GGML_OP_COUNT == 101, "GGML_OP_COUNT has changed - update RPC_PROTO_PATCH_VERSION");
 #endif
 
 #define GGML_RPC_MAX_SERVERS       16
